The original had `high = len(arr)` which caused an out-of-bounds access when `mid` pointed to index `len(arr)`, and also skipped the last element. The fix sets `high = len(arr) - 1` so the search range is `[0, len(arr)-1]`, matching standard inclusive bounds. In the `else` branch, we now set `high = mid - 1` instead of `high = mid` to correctly exclude the middle element.

